{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1371013-in-princess-the-hopeful-how-does-getting-married-affect-a-princess-if-at-all","id":1371013,"title":"In Princess: the Hopeful, how does getting married affect a Princess, if at all?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-28T07:37:19-08:00","id":1371013,"title":"In Princess: the Hopeful, how does getting married affect a Princess, if at all?","content":"Obviously it means she (or he) won't have as much time for adventuring, but are there any other mechanical or RP effects? Just wondering if any of you guys have played a game where this happened. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T05:49:46-08:00","id":1372684,"title":"","content":"There's no specific mechanical effect. The RP Effects are just what you'd think for having an SO. You have to choose between living a double life or coming clean with them. And of course, a spouse can prove a tempting target for the Darkness. Though they're obviously also a prime candidate to become a Sworn. Should note, there is a Princess the Hopeful Discord for questions.<br /> <br /> Don't forget, Princesses aren't necessarily adventurers. Many will pick up a job reflecting their Dream/Vocation. A Grace of Hearts being a politicians or a Seeker of Diamonds becoming a scientist isn't a really compromise with reality; they probably wouldn't have any other way. Troubadours easily have the skill (and magic) to pursue their art professionally. Menders will happily become doctors, with even the wanderlust prone Swords probably finding a spouse with a similar passion in the course of humanitarian work in an exotic, but destitute country. Even a Storms's spouse is probably a Stormwracked hunter/sworn any, and thus finds darkspawn killing a great idea for a date. Champions really have issue there, and most will probably pick a career where they can still help people - and of course, for a Champion Cop, they'll probably find out about more than a few taints in the course of duty to purify after hours.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25382-tzauri","name":"Tzauri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-04T08:49:33-08:00","id":1372720,"title":"","content":"Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T17:38:38-07:00","id":1385156,"title":"","content":"Just thought of something while reading this thread; if you were playing as a Noble and somehow discovered that you Girlfriend/Boyfriend/Spouse/Fiancee/Wife/Husband* was a supernatural creature^ (be it if they came clean, you unintentionally learn of it or they get transformed either sometime during the relationship or after the two of you tie the knot), how would your character react? As in, they were, or have become, a Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Leviathan, Genius or something else.<br /> <br /> *Delete as Appropriate<br /> ^If your ST is running a crossover game","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop